VERIFLOW-AICTE: Technical Architecture Audit for SIH 2026
================================================================

Document generated from codebase analysis on October 26, 2026.
Based on 112+ tool calls of source code review.

------------------------------------------------------------

1. TECHNOLOGY STACK
------------------------------------------------------------

1.1 Frontend Framework
- Next.js 14.2.15 with React 18.3.1
- Output mode: "standalone" for Docker self-contained bundle
- experimental.typedRoutes: false
- ReactStrictMode: true, poweredByHeader: false

1.2 Programming Languages
- TypeScript ^5.6.3 (full frontend type safety; tsc --noEmit clean)
- Python 3.11+ (backend)

1.3 UI Libraries and Styling
- Tailwind CSS 3.4.14 with custom design tokens
  Colors: seal red #A33A28, teal #0E4A45, turmeric #A97612,
  indigo #394A78, plum #6A3F5C
  Fonts: Spectral (serif), Public Sans (UI/sans-serif)
- tailwind-merge, tailwindcss-animate plugins
- Radix UI: avatar, dialog, dropdown-menu, progress, select,
  separator, slot, tabs, tooltip (all fully implemented)
- Lucide React icons
- Sonner toasts (^1.5.0)
- Recharts ^2.13.0 (SLA heatmap, funnel chart, KPI visualizations)
- Zod ^3.23.8 (schema validation, both frontend and backend via pydantic)
- React Hook Form ^7.53.1 with @hookform/resolvers
- @tanstack/react-query ^5.59.16 (server state caching, mutations,
  query devtools included)
- Axios ^1.7.7 (HTTP client to FastAPI backend)
- class-variance-authority ^0.7.0, clsx ^2.1.1
- next-themes ^0.3.0 (dark mode support)

1.4 Backend Framework and API Server
- FastAPI >=0.115.0,<1.0.0 (automatic OpenAPI docs, JSON validation,
  async endpoints)
- 15+ REST endpoints under /api/v1/:
  applications, documents, dashboard, workspace, auth,
  institutions, audit, workflow, deps

1.5 AI Models and External AI APIs
- Google Gemini gemini-2.5-flash via google-genai SDK >=1.0.0,<2.0.0
- ONLY AI API in the project (no OpenAI, no tesseract, no paddleOCR)
- Strict JSON response schema (LEASE_RESPONSE_SCHEMA) with 4 required fields:
  lease_start_date, lease_end_date, total_land_area_sqm, survey_numbers
- temperature=0.0, response_mime_type="application/json"
- Null return for ambiguous values; NEEDS_REVIEW for incomplete/contradictory
- Area unit conversion: 1 acre = 4046.8564224 m², 1 hectare = 10000 m²,
  1 sq ft = 0.09290304 m², 1 sq yd = 0.83612736 m² (internal _parse_area)

1.6 OCR and Document-Processing Libraries
- CONVENTIONAL OCR NOT USED (tesseract/paddleOCS not in codebase)
- All document processing goes through Gemini AI with deterministic
  post-validation
- Extraction results validated by code, not trusted blindly

1.7 Database and ORM
- PostgreSQL 16 (Docker) or SQLite (var/dev.db for local dev/tests)
- SQLAlchemy 2.0.35 (2.0 typed ORM; Mapped/mapped_column)
- Alembic >=1.13.3,<2.0.0 (migrations; Base.metadata target)
- psycopg >=3.2.3,<4.0.0 (postgresql+psycopg driver)
- greenlet >=3.1.1 (SQLAlchemy sync/async bridging)

1.8 Document and File Storage
- Local filesystem under var/uploads/ (default dev)
- S3/MinIO compatible via boto3 >=1.35.36,<2.0.0 (production/Docker)
- Storage backend selected by STORAGE_BACKEND env var:
  "local" or "s3"
- URI scheme: local://{key} or s3://{bucket}/{key}
- Max upload size: 25 MB
- SHA-256 content checksum stored per document

1.9 Workflow/State Management
- Custom state machine in workflow.py
- Linear: SCRUTINY → EVC → SAC → SHC → APPROVED|REJECTED
- NEW/EXPANSION → EVC mandatory; RENEWAL/CLOSURE → SAC direct
- Rule 1 (APH Cl. 2.1.e): live lease ≥ max course duration hard gate
- Rule 3: 15-day SLA dwell-time, clock restarts on every transition
- Every transition re-stamps stage_entry_timestamp (Rule 3)

1.9 Background Job Processing and Scheduling
- Celery >=5.4.0,<6.0.0 + Redis >=5.0.8,<6.0.0
- Celery beat sweeps SLA dwell times every minute
- Worker tasks: extract_document(), transition processing
- SLA alerts: L1 (dwell>15), L2 (dwell>30), L3 (dwell>45)

1.10 Notification Services
- Dashboard alerts and KPI tones only
- NO email/SMS/SLACK integration in prototype
- Escalation register viewable at /dashboard#escalations
- Seal tone (red) for SLA breached, teal for normal, turmeric for warnings

1.11 Authentication and Role-Based Access Control
- Officer model: email (unique, hashed password bcrypt), role,
  region_state, is_active, last_login_at
- JWT tokens on sign-in (shared password: veriflow@2026 for demos)
- Server-side role isolation (NOT UI hiding only):
  unauthenticated → 401; wrong-stage officer → 403 with message
  "This docket is not at your desk" or "This desk cannot make that move"
- 5 demo officers: scrutiny.officer, evc.member, sac.member,
  shc.member, ro.mumbai (regional oversight)
- No client secrets in project files; GEMINI_API_KEY via .env only

1.12 Deployment and Hosting Technologies
- Docker Compose: 6 services (db/Postgres 16, redis, api, worker,
  beat/SLA sweeper, web)
- backend/Dockerfile + frontend/Dockerfile
- Cloudflare Sites (per project configuration)
- NOT deployed via Vercel (despite skill entry in account)
- Environment variables in .env (never .dev.vars for GEMINI_API_KEY)
- Production: OPENAI_API_KEY via Cloud secret; on Sites → Secrets

1.13 Other Important Libraries and Services
- python-multipart >=0.0.12 (FastAPI multipart form uploads)
- email-validator >=2.2.0 (email format validation)
- PyJWT[crypto] >=2.9.0,<3.0.0 (JWT with crypto support)
- cryptography >=43.0.1 (token signing primitives)
- httpx >=0.27.2 + tenacity >=9.0.0 (resilient HTTP, Gemini requests)
- pytest >=8.3.3 + pytest-asyncio >=0.24.0 (59 passing tests)
- ruff >=0.6.9 (Python linting), mypy >=1.11.2 (type checking)

