2. ACTUAL SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE
------------------------------------------------------------

2.1 Flow: Frontend → Backend → Database

Next.js Frontend (TypeScript/Tailwind)
    │ (axios, JSON)
    ▼
FastAPI Backend (/api/v1/ endpoints)
    │
    ├─ POST /workspace/applications/{id}/transition
    │   └─ WorkflowService.transition() → state machine
    │       + Rule 1 gate + stage_entry_timestamp re-stamp
    │
    ├─ POST /documents/{id} (upload)
    │   │   └─ StorageService.put() → local/S3 → Document model
    │   │           └─ Celery task: extract_document()
    │   │                 └─ google.genai.Client → gemini-2.5-flash
    │   │                 │       └─ JSON schema validate
    │   │                 │           └─ apply_extraction() → DB
    │   │                 └─ AuditService.record() → SHA-256 chained
    │   │                           AuditLog
    │   │
    │   └─ GET /documents/{id}/details
    │       └─ WorkspaceDocumentRead + extraction_status
    │
    ├─ GET /workspace
    │   └─ WorkspaceService.build() → role-desk + KPIs + actions
    │
    └─ Regional SLA sweep (Celery beat every min)
        │
        ▼
PostgreSQL (SQLAlchemy 2.0 ORM)
    │   Tables: officers, institutions, applications, documents,
    audit_logs
    │   Indexes: status+stage_entry, documents.lease_end,
    uq_applications_inst_year_type_level
    ▼
Local FS or S3/MinIO (boto3)
    │   Document PDFs/Images: local://key or s3://bucket/key

2.2 API Endpoints (all under prefix="/api/v1")

Endpoint                    | Purpose                              | Auth
--------------------------|--------------------------------------|------
GET /workspace             | Officer's desk (dockets, facts, KPIs)| CurrentOfficer
POST /workspace/.../transition | Advance docket stage               | Role check
GET /documents/{id}        | List documents for application       | -
POST /documents/{id}       | Upload new document (multipart)      | -
GET /documents/{id}/details| Extraction status + lease snapshot   | -
GET /audit/timeline/{id}   | SHA-256 chained audit history        | -
GET /auth/login            | Sign-in, return JWT                  | -
GET /auth/me              | Current officer profile              | JWT

2.3 Upload Flow (detailed)

User selects file
  │
  ▼
Frontend: axios.post(/api/v1/documents, multipart/form-data)
  │
  ▼
Backend: StorageService.put(application_id, document_id,
  filename, data, mime_type)
  │
  ├─ local: write to var/uploads/{app_id}/{doc_id}-{filename}
  └─ s3: boto3.put_object(bucket, key, Body=data)
  │
  ▼
Document model row created:
  s3_url, mime_type, size_bytes, extraction_status=PENDING
  │
  ▼
Celery task: extract_document(db, document, actor="system:gemini")
  │
  ▼
GeminiLeaseExtractor.extract() → google.genai.Client.models.generate_content()
       │       response_schema=LEASE_RESPONSE_SCHEMA, temperature=0.0
       ▼
_text → _loads_json() → _validate() → LeaseExtraction dataclass
       │
       ├─ complete → extraction_status=EXTRACTED
       ├─ incomplete/contradictory → NEEDS_REVIEW
       └─ error → FAILED + extraction_error set
       │
       ▼
apply_extraction() → update Document.lease_start_date, .lease_end_date,
  .total_land_area_sqm, .survey_numbers, .extracted_json_data
  │
  ▼
AuditService.record(action="document.extracted" or
  "document.needs_review")
  │
  ▼
DB commit → docket now has lease data for Rule 1 evaluation

2.4 Workflow Flow (detailed)

Application enters → status=SCRUTINY + stage_entry_timestamp=now
  │
  ▼
Officer signs → role-based desk (Scrutiny/EVC/SAC/SHC/Regional)
  │
  ▼
Officer sees docket + permitted actions (from permitted_transitions
  + lease verdict)
  │
  ▼
Officer clicks move → POST /workspace/applications/{id}/transition
  │
  ▼
WorkflowService.transition()
  │
  ├─ Rule 1 gate: if SCRUTINY → EVC/SAC,
  evaluate_live_lease(db, application)
  │      → if not compliant → LeaseRuleBlocked error + audit entry
  │
  ├─ application.status = target
  ├─ stage_entry_timestamp = now  (Rule 3: SLA clock restarts)
  ├─ if TERMINAL: decided_at, decision_remarks
  │
  ▼
AuditService.record(action="stage.transition",
  previous_hash, sha256_hash chained)
  │
  ▼
db.commit() + db.refresh(application)
  │
  ▼
Frontend queue update → new docket state

2.5 SLA Dwell-Time Monitoring (detailed)

Application enters stage → stage_entry_timestamp recorded
  │
  ▼
Celery beat sweeps every minute (services/sla.py:sweep())
  │
  ▼: Query all apps where status IN ACTIVE_STAGES AND
  dwell_days > 15
  │
  ▼: Generate SlaAlertRead: level, dwell_days,
  institution_name, application_number, status, escalate_to
  │
  ▼: Store in DB → exposed to regional KPIs
  │
  ▼: Dashboard shows:
  • "Past SLA" KPI (seal tone if breached, teal if normal)
  • Escalation register link (/dashboard#escalations)
  • List of overdue dockets with floor(dwell_days)

------------------------------------------------------------

3. DOCUMENT INTELLIGENCE AND REGULATORY VALIDATION
------------------------------------------------------------

3.1 AI Model Used
- google-genai gemini-2.5-flash
- SDK: google.genai.Client
- Prompt: LEASE_PROMPT (30-line strict instruction with 5 rules)
- Schema: LEASE_RESPONSE_SCHEMA (4 required fields)
- Config: response_mime_type="application/json",
  response_schema=LEASE_RESPONSE_SCHEMA, temperature=0.0

3.2 Information Extracted from Documents
- lease_start_date (date, YYYY-MM-DD, or null)
- lease_end_date (date, YYYY-MM-DD, or null)
- total_land_area_sqm (float, positive, or null)
- survey_numbers (list of strings, each survey individually)
- extracted_json_data (raw Gemini JSON, audit trail)
- extraction_confidence (float, 0-1, penalized for issues)
- extraction_model (str, e.g. "gemini-2.5-flash")
- extraction_status (ExtractionStatus enum: PENDING/PROCESSING/
  EXTRACTED/NEEDS_REVIEW/FAILED)
- extraction_error (str, if failed)
- extracted_at (UTC timestamp)

3.3 OCR Usage
- CONVENTIONAL OCR NOT USED
- No tesseract, no paddleOCR, no open-source OCR library
- All processing through Gemini Vision with deterministic validation

3.4 Missing / Expired Document Detection
- Missing lease deed: document.doc_type != LEASE_DEED → ExtractionError
- Extraction failed: extraction_status=FAILED + error message
- Extraction needs review: extraction_status=NEEDS_REVIEW + badge color
  change + details show what missing/contradictory
- Lease expired: evaluate_live_lease() compares lease_end_date against
  current date + max_course_duration_years; if remaining_years <
  required_years → Rule 1 blocked

3.5 Cross-Document Inconsistencies
- No RAG/vector search or semantic similarity
- Inconsistencies detected by deterministic code comparing extracted
  fields:
  • lease_start_date/lease_end_date validity (end > start)
  • total_land_area_sqm > 0
  • survey_numbers not empty (confidence penalty)
  • Version deduplication: UniqueConstraint(
    "application_id", "doc_type", "version")
  prevents duplicate versions

3.6 APH Handbook Rules Representation and Evaluation

Rule 1 (APH Cl. 2.1.e): Live lease ≥ max course duration
  → evaluate_live_lease(db, application) in compliance.py
  → LeaseVerdict dataclass: compliant, reason, remaining_lease_years,
  required_lease_years, code
  → If not compliant → LeaseRuleBlocked error (workflow.py)
  → Move refused with specific reason shown in UI

Rule 2 (Triage): NEW/EXPANSION → EVC; RENEWAL/CLOSURE → SAC
  → EVC_REQUIRED_TYPES frozenset in workflow.py
  → allowed_transitions() returns permitted next states
  → Application type determines mandatory intermediate stage

Rule 3 (SLA): 15-day max per stage, clock restarts on transition
  → Application.dwell_days property (models.py)
  → is_sla_breached property (models.py)
  → Celery beat sweep every minute → SLA alerts
  → stage_entry_timestamp re-stamped on every transition

Rule 4 (Audit): SHA-256 chained append-only log
  → compute_audit_hash() (audit.py)
  → AuditLog.sha256_hash = SHA256(prev_hash || canonical_payload)
  → AuditLog.previous_hash links to prior entry
  → verify_chain(timeline) detects any modification retroactively
  → ondelete="RESTRICT" on all FKs (never hard-delete)

Rule 5 (Sequence competence): SCRUTINY→EVC→SAC→SHC→APPROVED/REJECTED
  → Linear state machine in allowed_transitions()
  → Terminal statuses: APPROVED, REJECTED (no further transitions)
  → InvalidTransition error with detailed context for illegal moves

3.7 Deterministic Post-AI Validation
- After Gemini extraction, code validates every field:
  • lease_end > lease_start (else NEEDS_REVIEW + issue)
  • total_land_area_sqm > 0 (else NEEDS_REVIEW + issue)
  • survey_numbers not empty (else confidence -0.1)
  • All four statutory fields present for EXTRACTED status
- If any validation fails → EXTRACTED cannot be set;
  status = NEEDS_REVIEW
- The AI is never trusted blindly; code is the source of truth

------------------------------------------------------------

4. WORKFLOW AUTOMATION
------------------------------------------------------------

4.1 Supported Application Stages

Stage       | Application Types | EVC Required | Moves Available
------------|-------------------|-------------|----------------
SCRUTINY    | ALL               | No (unless  | Forward to EVC
            |                   | NEW/EXPANS) | Forward to SAC
            |                   |             | Reject
EVC         | NEW, EXPANSION    | Yes (mandatory) | Send to SAC
            |                   |             | Send to SHC
SAC         | RENEWAL, CLOSURE  | No          | **Approve**
            |                   |             | **Reject**
            |                   |             | Send to SHC
SHC         | Referred from SAC | —           | **Approve**
            |                   |             | **Reject**
APPROVED    | Terminal          | —           | —
REJECTED    | Terminal          | —           | —

4.2 Workflow Selection Logic

Application.status + Application.application_type
    │
    ├─ SCRUTINY + NEW/EXPANSION → allowed: {EVC, REJECTED}
    │                         next_step: "Forward to EVC or straight to SAC"
    │
    ├─ SCRUTINY + RENEWAL/CLOSURE → allowed: {SAC, REJECTED}
    │                         next_step: "Forward to SAC"
    │
    ├─ EVC → allowed: {SAC, SHC}
    │                         next_step: "Recommend to SAC or refer to SHC"
    │
    ├─ SAC → allowed: {APPROVED, REJECTED, SHC}
    │                         next_step: "Approve/reject or refer to SHC"
    │
    └─ SHC → allowed: {APPROVED, REJECTED}
            next_step: "Approve or reject on record"

4.3 State Transition Validation

- Controlled by allowed_transitions() in workflow.py
- TERMINAL statuses (APPROVED/REJECTED) have no permitted transitions
- Application already in terminal → InvalidTransition error
- Target not in permitted → InvalidTransition with allowed list
- Concurrent decisions row-locked: db.refresh(app, with_for_update=True)
- Rule 1 gate on SCRUTINY moves (lease compliance)

4.4 Stage-Wise Pendency Calculation

dwell_days property (models.py):
  entered = as_utc(self.stage_entry_timestamp)
  return (utcnow() - entered).total_seconds() / 86_400

is_sla_breached property:
  return self.status in ACTIVE_STAGES and self.dwell_days > SLA_THRESHOLD_DAYS  # 15

4.5 Overdue Task Detection

- Celery beat sweep every minute
- Queries: status IN ACTIVE_STAGES AND dwell_days > 15
- Generates SlaAlertRead objects with level (L1/L2/L3 based on dwell days)
- L1: first breach (dwell>15), L2: second breach (dwell>30), L3: extreme (dwell>45)
- Alerts stored in DB → regional KPIs + escalation register

4.6 Escalation Levels and Recipients

Level | Condition                | Shown To           | Display
------|--------------------------|--------------------|--------
L1    | dwell_days > 15 (first)  | Regional KPIs      | "Past SLA" seal tone if any L1+
L2    | dwell_days > 30 (second) | Regional + desk    | Escalation register entry
L3    | dwell_days > 45 (extreme)| Higher authority   | Flag for immediate review

4.7 Notifications

- Dashboard alerts only (no email/SMS/SLACK)
- KPI tones: seal (breached), teal (normal), turmeric (warning)
- Escalation register at /dashboard#escalations lists all overdue
- No background job sends external notifications

4.8 Background Workers

- Celery worker: processes extract_document tasks, transition requests
- Celery beat: sweep SLA dwell times every minute
- Task example: extract_document(db_id, doc_id, actor, settings)
- Worker concurrency: default (prefork or eventlet)

------------------------------------------------------------

5. DATABASE, STORAGE, AND AUDIT
------------------------------------------------------------

5.1 Core Database Tables/Models

Model              | Key Fields                                                  | Relationships
------------------ |------------------------------------------------------------|--------------
officers           | id, email (unique), password_hash (bcrypt), role, region_state, is_active, is_active | 1:N → audit_logs
institutions       | id, aicte_permanent_id (unique), name, state, district, institution_type, approved_intake, is_autonomous | 1:N → applications
applications       | id, application_number (unique), institution_id, academic_year, application_type, programme_level, status, max_course_duration_years, stage_entry_timestamp, submitted_at, decided_at, decision_remarks | N:1 → institution, 1:N → documents, N:1 → latest audit_log
documents          | id, application_id, doc_type, version, file_name, s3_url, mime_type, size_bytes, content_sha256, extraction_status, extracted_json_data, lease_start_date, lease_end_date, total_land_area_sqm, survey_numbers | N:1 → application
audit_logs         | id, application_id, action, actor, actor_role, from_status, to_status, payload, timestamp, previous_hash, sha256_hash | N:1 → application

5.2 Main Application Entities and Relationships

- Institution: master regulator data (AICTE permanent ID, state, type)
- Application: one docket per institution/year/type/level (UniqueConstraint)
- Document: per-application files, extraction metadata, lease data
- Officer: signed-in identity + desk assignment (role = which stage)
- AuditLog: append-only, SHA-256 chained, tamper-evident

5.3 Where Uploaded Files Stored

- Default (dev): var/uploads/ directory
  Key format: {application_id}/{document_id}-{safe_filename}
  URI: local://{key}
  Public URL: {media_url_prefix}/{key}
- Production (Docker): S3/MinIO via boto3
  URI: s3://{bucket}/{key}
  Presigned URL expiry: configurable (default 24h)
- Metadata always in PostgreSQL (Document table), never in file

5.4 Document Metadata Separate from File

- YES: extraction_status, extracted_json_data (raw Gemini JSON),
  lease_start_date, lease_end_date, total_land_area_sqm,
  survey_numbers, extraction_confidence, extraction_model,
  extracted_at, extraction_error all stored in Document row
- File binary stored externally (local/S3). Metadata always in PG.

5.5 Workflow History Recording

- SHA-256 chained AuditLog entries per application
- Each entry: action, actor, actor_role, from_status, to_status,
  payload (structured), timestamp, previous_hash, sha256_hash
- Serialised writes: _lock_chain(application_id) → PostgreSQL
  pg_advisory_xact_lock prevents concurrent fork
- verify_chain(timeline) returns (valid, first_error)
- Never hard-deleted: ondelete="RESTRICT" on all FKs

5.6 Integrity Mechanism

- SHA-256 hash chaining: each AuditLog entry's sha256_hash =
  SHA256(previous_hash || canonical_payload_of_this_entry)
- Previous hash links form immutable chain per application
- Verification possible via AuditService.verify(application_id)
- NOT enforced as DB-immutable (code supports verification, but
  DB admin could theoretically bypass); described as "append-only
  with SHA-256 chaining" not "tamper-proof by design"

5.7 Security Controls

- Officer auth: bcrypt password hash + JWT token
- Role-based desk isolation: server-side (401/403 on boundary crossing)
- Document ownership: Application → Institution link; no client-supplied IDs in queries
- SLA queries: indexed via ix_applications_status_stage_entry
- No secrets in frontend or git; all keys via .env only

