7. ARCHITECTURE DIAGRAM SPECIFICATION (4 LAYERS)
------------------------------------------------------------

Layer 1: PRESENTATION LAYER
- Next.js 14 + React 18 + Tailwind CSS + Radix UI
- Sign-in page, dashboards, desk views, document upload
- Recharts for KPI/SLA visualizations
- Sonner toasts, Zod schema validation
- Connection: HTTP (axios, JSON) → Application Layer

Layer 2: APPLICATION LAYER
- FastAPI with 15+ /api/v1/ endpoints
- CurrentOfficer dependency, role checks
- Multipart form handling (document upload)
- Workflow transition validation (state machine)
- Connection: HTTP → Service Layer; SQLAlchemy ORM → Data Layer

Layer 3: SERVICE LAYER
- Core business logic
- WorkflowService — state machine + Rules 1/2/3 validation
- AuditService — SHA-256 chained append-only log
- StorageService — local/S3 document read/write
- GeminiLeaseExtractor — google-genai document extraction
- SlaService — Celery beat sweeper + 15-day alerts
- PermissionsService — permitted_transitions + desk custody
- ComplianceService — evaluate_live_lease()
- Connection: Direct imports from FastAPI endpoints; Celery/Redis for background

Layer 4: DATA LAYER
- PostgreSQL 16 via SQLAlchemy 2.0 ORM
- Tables: officers, institutions, applications, documents, audit_logs
- UUID primary keys, Alembic migrations
- Indexes: status+stage_entry, documents.lease_end,
  uq_applications_inst_year_type_level
- ondelete="RESTRICT" on all FKs (never hard-delete)
- Connection: SQL queries → PostgreSQL; Celery worker writes to PG

Infrastructure Layer (below Data):
- Docker Compose: db, redis, api, worker, beat, web
- backend/Dockerfile + frontend/Dockerfile
- Environment variables: .env (GEMINI_API_KEY, DB URL, storage config)
- MinIO / local filesystem for object storage

Layer connections:
Presentation → Application (HTTP)
Application → Service (direct imports)
Service → Data (SQLAlchemy ORM → PostgreSQL)
Service → Infrastructure (Celery/Redis for background tasks)
Infrastructure → Data (worker writes to PG, reads from Redis)
Data → Service (triggered by writes; rule re-evaluation on DB write)

