C. THE FIVE MOST IMPORTANT TECHNICAL FEATURES

1. SHA-256 chained audit log — Every application transition is
   cryptographically linked, enabling retroactive integrity verification.
   No generic doc-management system has this for statutory workflows.

2. Role-based desk isolation enforced server-side — 5 officer roles each
   get a completely separate workspace with distinct permitted moves.
   Crossing stage boundaries returns 403, not just UI hiding. Verified in
   API tests (unauthenticated→401, wrong stage→403 with specific message).

3. Gemini AI with deterministic post-validation — The model extracts
   lease deed data under strict JSON schema; if ambiguous → null; if
   contradictory → NEEDS_REVIEW. Final Rule 1 compliance is checked by
   code, not the AI. "AI only organizes, officer decides" is core.

4. 15-day SLA dwell-time with automated escalation — Celery beat
   sweeps all active dockets every minute. dwell_days > 15 triggers
   seal-tone KPI + escalation register. Rule 3 fully automated, not just
   displayed.

5. Statutory state machine with Rule gates — Scrutiny→EVC→SAC→SHC→
   APPROVED/REJECTED, with NEW/EXPANS→EVC mandatory, RENEWAL/CLOSURE→
   SAC direct. Rule 1 (lease live ≥ course duration) hard-gates moves
   out of Scrutiny. SLA clock restarts on every transition.

D. KEY IMPLEMENTATION DETAILS DISTINGUISHING VERIFLOW-AICTE

1. AI is purely advisory — Gemini extracts lease data; every move/
   decision is signed by an officer into the SHA-256 audit chain. The
   system is designed so the AI never has authority to approve/reject/
   advance. This architecturally distinguishes it from doc-management
   systems that use AI to auto-approve.

2. Rule 1 (APH Cl. 2.1.e) is a code-gated hard constraint —
   LeaseRuleBlocked error with specific reason prevents any docket from
   leaving Scrutiny without a valid lease. The check runs as part of the
   workflow service, not as a separate validation step.

3. Each phase has its own desk + login — 5 demo officers, each with
   separate credentials and completely different dockets based on their
   stage. Server-side isolation (CurrentOfficer dependency +
   stage_for_role()) means the same docket ID means different things in
   different desks.

4. SLA dwell timer restarts on every transition —
   stage_entry_timestamp = timestamp on every transition(). This means
   a docket dwelling 20 days in Scrutiny, then moving to EVC, then to
   SAC, gets a fresh 15-day clock at each stage. dwell_days computes
   days in current stage only.

5. No conventional OCR — All document processing goes through Gemini
   gemini-2.5-flash with strict schema. The codebase explicitly does not
   use tesseract/paddleOCR. The AI both reads and validates (returns
   null for missing fields), making the system deterministic after
   extraction.

E. DISCREPANCIES Between Documented Architecture and Actual Code

| Documented Claim                    | Actual Code Reality                                              |
|-------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Uses Supabase for DB/auth           | No Supabase references anywhere. PostgreSQL via SQLAlchemy +     |
|                                     | bcrypt-hashed passwords + JWT.                                   |
| Uses tesseract OCR for document reading | Not in codebase. All extraction goes through Google Gemini.      |
| Has email/SMS notifications         | Only dashboard alerts. No external messaging integration.         |
| Has real-time WebSocket updates     | Polling-based. useWorkspace() refetched on interval; no true     |
|                                     | WebSocket or SSE.                                                |
| Deployed via Vercel                 | Deployed via Cloudflare Sites or Docker. No Vercel integration.  |
| Uses Next.js API routes only        | Dedicated FastAPI backend; Next.js app/ has minimal routes.      |
| Audit log is tamper-proof by design | Code supports verification (verify_chain()) but not enforcement. |
|                                     | DB admin could bypass; described as "append-only with SHA-256    |
|                                     | chaining" not "tamper-proof by design".                          |
| Uses MinIO for production storage   | Configurable via STORAGE_BACKEND env var: "local" (default dev) |
|                                     | or "s3" (Docker production). Local is the default.               |
| Uses Supabase Auth                  | No Supabase; bcrypt-hashed passwords + JWT custom implementation.|

